# DARIA's synchroniser marks (POCKET_DARIA; docs/DARIA_CORE.md 7.1-7.3).
#
# Loaded only by its QIP_FILE line in ap_core.qsf, one of the three DARIA
# lines; a build without DARIA drops it and keeps its instance assignments
# as they were. The marks themselves, 16 SYNCHRONIZER_IDENTIFICATION FORCED
# instance assignments on the first flops of plan 2.7's synchronisers, are
# in daria_sync.tcl beside this file, which this file sources: Quartus
# refuses SYNCHRONIZER_IDENTIFICATION in a qip (it tags each assignment of a
# qip with -qip, an option that assignment does not take), and takes it from
# a sourced Tcl file. See daria_sync.tcl. So does the DARIA build's one
# fitter setting, ROUTER_REGISTER_DUPLICATION OFF (the guard's pd_tog and
# pd_rx kept single registers), at the end of daria_sync.tcl.

set_global_assignment -name SOURCE_TCL_SCRIPT_FILE [file join $::quartus(qip_path) daria_sync.tcl]
